+   chains (PR120687).  All other operand sets may be reordered freely;
+   in particular the operand grouping performed by
+   swap_ops_for_binary_stmt is what enables pass_optimize_bswap (which
+   runs before the late reassoc pass) to recognize byte-swap and
+   rotate idioms written as shift/and/or chains (PR121298).  */
